### Login as admin
# @name adminLogin
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan@admin.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Login as client
# @name clientLogin
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}


### 1- Admin creates a service (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/services
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Beard trim",
  "durationMinutes": 20
}

### 2- Admin repeats the same service (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/services
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Beard trim",
  "durationMinutes": 20
}

### 3- Client tries create (expect 403)
POST http://localhost:3000/services
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{clientLogin.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Beard trim",
  "durationMinutes": 20
}

### 4- No token (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/services
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Beard trim",
  "durationMinutes": 20
}

### 5- Duration with text (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/services
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Hair cut",
  "durationMinutes": "30"
}

### 6- List active services (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/services
